This product uses the following third-party software and ideas.

FreeLLMAPI (https://github.com/tashfeenahmed/freellmapi), MIT licence, Copyright (c) the FreeLLMAPI authors.
  Jarvis's provider router follows several ideas first seen in FreeLLMAPI: reading the wait time a provider asks for from the
  Retry-After header, the JSON error body and plain prose (router/retry.js); per-key request and token quota windows with UTC-day
  reset (router/ledger.js); an exponentially decaying reliability score and first-word timing (router/health.js); rescuing tool calls
  that a model writes as text (tools/rescue.js). The code in this repository is a fresh implementation written for Jarvis; no
  FreeLLMAPI source file is copied.

sherpa-onnx (https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx), Apache License 2.0.
  Speech recognition, text to speech and keyword spotting run through the sherpa-onnx-node package.

Models downloaded on demand (never bundled), each with its own licence shown before download:
  Moonshine base English (MIT); sherpa-onnx KWS zipformer gigaspeech (Apache-2.0); Piper voice "Alan" en_GB (see the voice's MODEL_CARD).

piper-phonemize-node (GPL-3.0-or-later), downloaded as a separate optional component and loaded at run time. It is not linked into
  or distributed with Jarvis. It is only needed for the Piper natural voice; without it Jarvis uses the Windows voice.

Electron (MIT), electron-updater (MIT).
